== Availability

By design, a failed task, a broker outage or an identity outage loses no committed payment or event (AD-04, AD-06). On 13–14 November 2026 on AWS, controlled V5 task replacement and V7 poison-message drills passed within the tested configurations below, but identity R1 failed and payment/replay remained unexecuted; AISS-13 is partially resolved, not closed. The successful identity/poison rehearsal of 15 October remains local historical evidence, not current AWS acceptance. The database, the Valkey node and the NAT instance each run in one zone, so a zone failure still stops purchases, sign-ins or outbound calls (AISS-01). @tbl-availability-failures lists each failure, what recovers it and whether we saw it on AWS or locally.

*Application recovery.* On 16 October on AWS, two healthy commerce tasks ran in different zones. That deployment passed its smoke suite at 14:10 SGT only after an interrupted start and a manual repair of suspended scaling targets (#src("docs/swe5001/evidence/20261016-http-baseline-dashboard/README.md")[placement record], AISS-14). The ALB routes only to healthy targets, and ECS keeps the desired task count (AD-07, AD-08). The deployment circuit breaker rolls an unhealthy deployment back to the last completed one (#src("infra/swe5001/modules/ecs-service/main.tf")[ECS service module]). V5's controlled result follows. Configured, not tested: V6 (a bad release rolled back) was not run on AWS.

*V5 controlled task replacement.* On 13 November 2026 on AWS, V5 R3 passed: *60,000 workload GETs* plus one setup GET, with zero invalid/non-2xx responses, browse errors or dropped iterations. After the approved task stop under load, the first source-bound ALB-healthy observation was at *79.458 s*, within the unchanged *120 s* limit; this is an observation time, not an exact health-transition instant. The tested correction was commerce *1,024 CPU units / 2,048 MiB*, a pool of *five* connections and *120 s* ALB slow start; it does not pass R2's smaller configuration, whose errors and *155 s* replacement failure remain retained. R1's interrupted workload also remains failed. V5 used released application `3a893036` with separately recorded tooling and runtime corrections, not the later experimental V4 R5 image. Source: `20261114-v4-r5-live/v5-r3-pass.md` and its adjacent `working-report-addendum.md` under the evidence directory in §2.2, which states the working-draft publication boundary.

